Introduction
Multimodal learning to bridge vision and language has gained broad interest from both the computer vision and natural language processing communities. Significant progress has been made in many vision-language tasks, including image-text matching<|CIT-MASK|>, visual captioning<|CIT-MASK|>, visual grounding<|CIT-MASK|> and visual question answering (VQA)<|CIT-MASK|>. Compared to other multimodal learning tasks, VQA is a more challenging task that requires fine-grained semantic understanding of both the image and the question, together with visual reasoning to predict an accurate answer.

